    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d370-a9">

                <pb facs="0815" n="805" sameAs="frus:frus1864p1/pg805"/>

                <head> [(I.)—<hi rendition="#italic">Circular to consuls and consular
                    agents.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of
                            State,</hi>
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#italic">Richmond,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-06-10"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >June</hi> 10, 1863</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> It becomes my duty to inform you that the
                    president has determined to permit no direct communication between consuls or
                    consular agents of foreign countries residing within the confederacy, and the
                    functionaries of such foreign governments residing in the enemy’s lines. The
                    passage, in future, of consular couriers, messengers, or of consuls or consular
                    agents themselves, through the confederate lines to the enemy, is accordingly
                    prohibited, and foreign officials will be allowed to communicate with their
                    governments only directly, or through neutral countries.</p>
                <p>With great respect, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>J. P. BENJAMIN.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
